From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Erik Bourget <erik@ebourget.net>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 01:53:02 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] dt-bindings: iommu: apple,dart: Add apple,bypass-sids

A USB4 PCIe tunnel DART has reserved streams that its PCIe-C port issues
its own writes on, such as the interrupt controller writes its MSIs turn
into. List those streams so they are set to bypass.

Signed-off-by: Erik Bourget <erik@ebourget.net>
(cherry picked from commit 2682b17dc76d98f4e6838aa9e6e3f798b8d570b9)
---
 .../devicetree/bindings/iommu/apple,dart.yaml         | 11 +++++++++++
 1 file changed, 11 insertions(+)

diff --git a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/iommu/apple,dart.yaml b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/iommu/apple,dart.yaml
index 865cd9584b..7b5e275e02 100644
--- a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/iommu/apple,dart.yaml
+++ b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/iommu/apple,dart.yaml
@@ -129,6 +129,17 @@ properties:
       Tree by the bootloader and required to initialize dynamically powered
       DART instances.
 
+  apple,bypass-sids:
+    $ref: /schemas/types.yaml#/definitions/uint32-array
+    minItems: 1
+    maxItems: 8
+    items:
+      maximum: 255
+    description:
+      Reserved streams of a USB4 PCIe tunnel DART that its PCIe-C port issues
+      its own writes on, such as the interrupt controller writes its MSIs
+      turn into. They are set to bypass after every reset of the DART.
+
   apple,remap-streams:
     $ref: /schemas/types.yaml#/definitions/uint32-matrix
     minItems: 1
